<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    DEPRECATED for IVS credentials.

    The IVS ingest endpoint, stream key, and chat room ARN are NO LONGER read by
    the app. They are secrets that must live only on the backend and are handed to
    authenticated creators at runtime by the `createStreamCredentials` Cloud
    Function. Set them there instead:

        firebase functions:secrets:set IVS_INGEST_ENDPOINT
        firebase functions:secrets:set IVS_STREAM_KEY
        firebase functions:secrets:set IVS_CHAT_ROOM_ARN

    If a stream key was ever committed or shipped in a build, ROTATE it in the AWS
    IVS console — a leaked key lets anyone broadcast to the channel.

    This template is retained only for any future client-side, non-sensitive
    configuration values.
-->
